==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|lickedy-split}}

===Etymology===
First attested during the 19th century, in the US, equivalent to {{com|en|lickedy|split}}, perhaps as a reference to the flick of a snake's tongue. The forms {{m|en|lickety-cut}} and {{m|en|licketie}} are similarly attested; and forms with ''t'' are likely due to Scottish influence.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-lickety-split.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[quickly|Quickly]]; as [[fast]] as possible; in short order.
#: ''At the sound of the starting gun, they were off and running '''lickety-split'''.''
#: ''I need tea right now, '''lickety-split'''.''
